---
import ManualLayout from '../../layouts/ManualLayout.astro';
import { chapters, manualLink } from '../../lib/manual';
---

<ManualLayout title="jk manual"
  description="Inspect and edit Jujutsu repositories from a terminal interface."
  eyebrow="Using jk">
  <div class="manual-intro">
    <p>Use the log to select changes and inspect their contents. Rebase, squash, and restore show
      the affected revisions before you confirm; New and Edit run immediately.</p>
    <a class="manual-start" href={manualLink('start')}>Open your first repository <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <h2 id="workflows">Follow a workflow</h2>
  <ol class="manual-chapter-list">
    {chapters.map((chapter, index) => (
      <li><a href={manualLink(chapter.slug)}>
        <span class="manual-chapter-number">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <span><strong>{chapter.title}</strong><span>{chapter.description}</span></span>
        <span class="manual-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a></li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <h2 id="look-up-a-command">Look up a command</h2>
  <p>Find a command's keys, options, and effects in the
    <a href={manualLink('reference')}>command reference</a>. Entries distinguish native actions,
    commands run with <code>:</code>, and commands that require a separate terminal.</p>
  <div class="manual-callout">
    <strong><a href={manualLink('recordings')}>Recorded workflows</a></strong>
    <p>Watch rebase, bookmark, and recovery examples in disposable repositories. Each recording
      includes screenshots, terminal text, and checks of the resulting repository.</p>
  </div>
  <h2 id="current-boundaries">Current boundaries</h2>
  <p>jk 0.3.0 includes whole-change rebase, squash, and restore previews, bookmarks and remotes,
    workspace management, command history, and operation recovery. Native partial-change editing,
    conflict resolution, and real push remain gaps. The <a href={manualLink('audit')}>UX findings</a>
    describe the evidence and proposed improvements.</p>
</ManualLayout>
